     That sacrafice behavior predates the introduction of the
Riders.  (If protecting their corpses had been the reason, adding
auto-revival for #offer like for pick-up would have been a better
choice.)  I'm pretty sure that it was done that way so that Amulets
could be included as likely candidates when you respond with ? to
the "offer what?" prompt.  Offering things off the ground is limited
to corpses, although whoever decided on only-from-inventory for high
altars could have modified the floor item processing instead.

     There have been some changes to this in the post-3.4.3
development code.  Offering corpses off the floor at high altars
will work, and attempting to offer an amulet from inventory at any
non-high altar will actually do something instead of just saying
"you can't do that".  (There's been some sacrifice code to handle
this for a long time, but inventory selection for #offer prevented
it from getting used).  I don't recall offhand whether the changes
go far enough to offer amulets off the floor.


